# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — never commit. See docs/05-stack.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

web/dist/
# Where `shellDigest` measures the shell, away from `web/dist` so a parallel browser suite
# cannot overwrite what it is reading (2026-08-16). Removed by the function itself; ignored
# here so a crashed run cannot leave a committable directory behind.
web/.digest/
web/.digest-files/

# Real contact data. Never committed.
#
# Personal mobile numbers of named district officials are operational data, not source.
# Git history is permanent and hard to purge, and a private repo can be shared, forked or
# have a collaborator added later. These live in the database, and reach it through a seed
# file that stays out of the repository — the same rule as .env.
*.docx

# `**/` is load-bearing. A gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory
# holding the .gitignore, so `db/seed/*.json` matches only `<root>/db/seed/` — and the real
# file lives at `app/db/seed/`. The first version of this rule silently matched nothing and
# would have committed the contact list a second time. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
**/db/seed/*.json
!**/db/seed/*.example.json

# Evidence files. The record of them is in the database; the bytes are not the repo's.
app/var/

# Cookie jars written by curl while poking at the local server. A live session token is a
# credential even when it is only good against 127.0.0.1 (M4, 2026-08-03 — one reached a
# commit and had to be pulled back out before it was pushed).
app/cook.txt
*.cookies
cookies.txt

# Notes scribbled while standing up an account, with the credentials still in them. Cloudflare
# shows an R2 secret access key exactly once, so it gets pasted somewhere before it is put in
# `.env` — and that somewhere was this folder, untracked and unignored, on 2026-08-08. The real
# home for every one of these values is `app/.env`; a file like this is a copy that outlives its
# reason. Named explicitly rather than by a `*.txt` sweep, which would also swallow real notes.
r2 bukket.txt

# The release build. Everything under these two is generated by `installer/build-installer.ps1`
# and none of it is source.
#
# `stage/` is the load-bearing one: it holds a copy of `db/seed/directory.json`, so committing
# it would put ~40 officials' personal mobile numbers into git history by a second route, after
# the rule above was written specifically to stop that happening once. It also carries a Node
# runtime and a PostgreSQL server — 200 MB of somebody else's binaries.
#
# `out/` is the finished setup.exe and the ZIP, which contain the same directory file inside
# them. The release goes to the district directly; it does not go through the repository.
installer/stage/
installer/out/

# The Activities porting kit (PLAN §7): generated, read-only hand-over, never source.
/port-kit/
